I've spent the past 25 years doing open source consultancy and engineering management for 
Stone-IT, X-Tend and Inuits/o11y .  I've build infrastructures with open source tooling that could 
survive the 10th floor test, or rather the OVH Fire.   

More recently I've coached different organisations, ranging from startups to large internatonal banks  to adopt devops practices, and thus also agile practices,  
While changing organisation is a  very interesting challenge, I was always happier on the days I was back at building or debugging technology  with a team, 

So I`m back to a more technical opensource engineering leadership role.  Back to a community  that I knew quite good  almost 2 
decades ago , the larger MySQL community,  while also getting back involved into the Open Sourcer Obervabillity community.   

Last month I started at Percona as their Practice Lead for Observability,  I`ll be leading the effort to both have better observability features in our tools, but also helping 
customers to get better insights in  their ecosystems. 






